codex
The semantics has direct support for integer comparisons, list iteration, `len`, subscripting, and function frames. I’m using a cyclic-descent implementation: a nonempty list is a rotation of ascending order exactly when its circular sequence has at most one strict descent. This avoids relying on the semantics’ trusted opaque `sorted` primitive and gives the proof a structural loop invariant.
